    {
      "id": "IMAGE_REUSE",
      "detail": "Existing image1729 was created at 08:07 UTC and reused by exact immutable local image ID with --pull=never. Recipe107c is the pinned upstream base manifest, not that local image object. Retained build log binds the base/checksummed Foundry and solc additions to image1729. No fresh-image build or independent image rebuild is claimed."
    },
    {
      "id": "FRESHNESS_EVIDENCE",
      "detail": "Source preparation logs/reflog show a new --no-hardlinks local clone and exact local top-level submodule clones. Empty cache before installation and absent pre-install node_modules are operator-recorded preparation facts, not states retrospectively re-observable after installation. Reviewer independently confirms empty npm configs now, distinct clone/no alternates, a real npm ci install log, and installed lock entries consistent with committed versions/resolved/integrity. No host dependency-tree copy is in the recorded commands."
    },
    {
      "id": "VENDOR_NESTED_SUBMODULES",
      "detail": "The two required top-level gitlinks are exact and clean. Three OpenZeppelin nested test-only gitlinks remain uninitialized; no recursive-submodule completeness is asserted. The pinned Foundry recipe disables auto-remappings and maps only forge-std/src and OpenZeppelin/contracts."
    },
    {
      "id": "NETWORK_BOUNDARY",
      "detail": "Install/audit intentionally use Docker bridge with the managed proxy/CA and explicit npm strict TLS/HTTPS registry. This config is not a per-domain firewall proof. Foundation/journey use --network=none with no published ports and no proxy/CA/credential mounts, while loopback fixtures remain available."
    },
    {
      "id": "WRITABLE_WORKSPACE",
      "detail": "Root filesystem is read-only; the owned source/output binds are intentionally writable for dependencies and build results. Post-run tracked source and lock remain clean. This is not a claim that ignored generated outputs never change."
    }
